cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this repository, please cite it using these metadata. Code is MIT-licensed; text, protocols,
  coding sheets, the paper table and aggregate results are CC BY 4.0 (see LICENSE and LICENSE-CC-BY-4.0).
title: "Life science at ML venues: reproducibility practice and agentic reproduction of medical and life-science papers"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kondrateva
    given-names: Ekaterina
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3623-6106"
    affiliation: Hertie AI Institute for Brain Health, University of Tübingen; Maastricht University
  - family-names: Kofler
    given-names: Florian
    affiliation: Hertie AI Institute for Brain Health, University of Tübingen; University of Zurich; Technical University of Munich; Helmholtz Munich
  - family-names: Simkó
    given-names: Attila
    affiliation: Umeå University
repository-code: "https://github.com/kondratevakate/life-science-at-ml-venues"
abstract: >-
  A systematic meta-research study of 2,170 medical and life-science papers and an equal random sample of other
  papers at nine venue-years of CVPR, ICCV, ECCV, ICLR, ICML and NeurIPS (2025-2026): twelve reproducibility
  practices coded from 3,278 full texts under a frozen protocol, and reproduction outcomes from the ICML 2026 agent
  reproduction challenge.
keywords:
  - reproducibility
  - meta-research
  - medical machine learning
  - life science
  - agentic reproduction
license: MIT
